                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I first was like -meh-\n\nThe motion system is weird, there are not a lot of environnements, only one game mode, ... I tried the tutorial and already thought about a refund.\nBut then I started a multiplayer game, and I had one of the funniest time with my Vive to this date. I literally laughed my ass off at some times. \n\nThe game is straight forward, totally no-brainer.\nYou scan the area to locate players and weapons, then dig your way to them by moving and punching cubes.\nYou die a lot and frag a lot.\n\nPROs :\n- Easy to play, games are fast paced, it's instant fun.\n- Lots of (funny) weapons, \n- Environnements are fully destructible. They are just filled cubes made of smaller cubes, and you shape your playground with fists, bullets and explosions. \n- lots of masks to unlock (I don't know how yet, though).\n\n\nCONs:\n- There doesn't seem to need a lot of strategy nor skill... But that means that anyone can have fun, no Munchkin nor powergaming.\n- The motion system is weird (you move \"step by step\" forward or backward with no transition), but at least it prevents from motion sickness. I don't understand why you're not allowed to move laterally, though. \n- Everything is destructible, even covers, so roomscale covering and ducking do not seem to be that useful (you die too fast anyway).\n- The immersion is not the best I've seen (everything goes fast and moves are jerky, dodging and ducking seems useless -see above-, that does not helps make you really feel like \"you are there\") but the fun and clarity are there. \n\n\nSome moments to help you better understand why I recommend this game:\n\n- Stealing the weapon from the hand of your enemy while he is using it, and frantically punching him in the face while he desperately tries to steal it back (seriously, this should be a norm in all shooters this is hilarious). \n- Dodging bullets with a frying pan, and repeatedly knocking your adversary on the top of the head with it... And winning... \n- Throwing a grenade right in front of an enemy who hasn't noticed you, observing him watching it, freaking out, trying to flee then exploding. One Tex-Avery moment. \n- Targeting an enemy with a scan through the wall with a rocket launcher, that digs a tunnel right to the target who never saw it coming. \n\n\n",
